# Views and URLs

- Function-based and typed: `HttpRequest` in, `HttpResponse` out. Subclass a
  Django CBV only for auth flows and other security-sensitive built-ins.
- Early return on method checks. POST/redirect/GET after a successful write.
- `get_object_or_404` with an ownership-scoped queryset; never a bare
  `objects.get(pk=request.GET[...])`.
- `select_related` / `prefetch_related` for anything the template walks.
- Real status codes: 400 invalid, 403 forbidden, 404 missing. No 200 with an
  error buried in the body.
- App `urls.py` sets `app_name`; `api_urls.py` does **not** (the version
  namespace owns it). Reverse by name, never hardcode a path.

See skills: `django-views-urls`, `htmx-patterns`, `django-rest-framework`.
